%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 24cee7e49fc532a45ab71bd5ace6cb7b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Stage1Tutorial
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: As you know, waking a well takes 'oasis sand'. It's special stuff,
      and there's only ever so much of it.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC54C\uB2E4\uC2DC\uD53C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC744 \uB6AB\uAE30 \uC704\uD574\uC120
      '\uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798'\uB77C\uB294 \uD2B9\uC218\uD558\uACE0
      \uD55C\uC815\uB41C \uC790\uC6D0\uC744 \uC368\uC57C \uB3FC\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b01f092eb0545574db7d43f93e64aba7, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: But why do we use sand, of all things, to wake a well? I still
      don't get it.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uADFC\uB370, \uC65C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC744 \uB6AB\uB294 \uB370
      \uB610 \uBAA8\uB798\uB97C \uC368\uC57C \uB418\uC9C0? \uC544\uC9C1\uB3C4 \uC774\uD574\uAC00
      \uC548 \uB418\uB124."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a27f087f63d32394aa6a316793fe64ae, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: ...You've been doing this for three years and you're asking me
      that now?
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "...\uC774 \uC77C\uC744 3\uB144\uC774\uB098 \uD588\uB2E4\uBA74\uC11C
      \uAC11\uC790\uAE30 \uADF8\uB7F0 \uC18C\uB9AC\uB97C \uD558\uB294 \uAC70\uC608\uC694?"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b0c713d599beb9344b4ee106a4240d3b, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: It shocks the dry ground so the water deep down can find a way
      up, or something. That's roughly how it works, right?
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uBA54\uB9C8\uB978 \uB545\uC5D0 \uC790\uADF9\uC744 \uC918\uC11C
      \uAE4A\uC219\uD55C \uACF3\uC5D0 \uC788\uB294 \uBB3C\uAE38\uC744 \uC704\uB85C
      \uD2B8\uC774\uAC8C \uD558\uB294 \uBB50... \uB300\uCDA9 \uADF8\uB7F0 \uC6D0\uB9AC\uC758
      \uC18C\uC7AC \uC544\uB2C8\uC5C8\uC5B4\uC694?"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b0c713d599beb9344b4ee106a4240d3b, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: Very roughly. Still don't get it.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB108\uBB34 \uB300\uCDA9\uC778\uB370. \uC5EC\uC804\uD788 \uC774\uD574\uAC00
      \uC548 \uAC00."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 09aff2867ae9ee3479addb17d5a880eb, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Anyway, oasis sand can only be dropped here, inside this area.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC544\uBB34\uD2BC \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB294
      \uC5EC\uAE30 \uC774 \uBD80\uBD84, \uC774 \uC601\uC5ED \uC548\uC5D0\uB9CC \uB5A8\uC5B4\uD2B8\uB9B4
      \uC218 \uC788\uC5B4\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b01f092eb0545574db7d43f93e64aba7, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: There's a limit to how much you can use at once, so spend it
      carefully, a bit at a time!
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uD55C \uBC88\uC5D0 \uC4F8 \uC218 \uC788\uB294 \uC591\uC740
      \uC815\uD574\uC838 \uC788\uC73C\uB2C8, \uC870\uAE08\uC529 \uC2E0\uC911\uD558\uAC8C
      \uC0AC\uC6A9\uD574\uC57C \uB3FC\uC694!"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce46d5e3f69096f4a84f9897353ff324, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: Right. Controlling the amount is the whole trick. You're much
      better at that than me.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB9DE\uC544. \uC591 \uC870\uC808\uC744 \uC798\uD558\uB294 \uAC8C
      \uD575\uC2EC\uC774\uC57C. \uADF8\uAC74 \uB098\uBCF4\uB2E4 \uB108\uAC00 \uD6E8\uC52C
      \uB354 \uC798\uD558\uB294 \uAC83 \uAC19\uC544."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 45ba7650e66fc1349bc111d80a881bb0, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Once you've used a certain amount of oasis sand, mud builds up
      in response.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC77C\uC815\uB7C9\uC758 \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB97C
      \uC0AC\uC6A9\uD558\uACE0 \uB098\uBA74, \uADF8\uC5D0 \uB300\uD55C \uBC18\uC751\uC73C\uB85C
      \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC5EC\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 312af029b1b084a41ade9a6fdf1a6418, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: Mud is a good sign. It means the ground is getting wet. But let
      too much pile up in one spot and it plugs the well right back up.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC9C4\uD759\uC740 \uB545\uC774 \uBB3C\uC5D0 \uC816\uACE0 \uC788\uB2E4\uB294
      \uC88B\uC740 \uC2E0\uD638\uC9C0\uB9CC, \uBC18\uB300\uB85C \uD55C \uACF3\uC5D0
      \uB108\uBB34 \uC313\uC774\uBA74 \uB3C4\uB85C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC774 \uB9C9\uD600\uBC84\uB824."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a27f087f63d32394aa6a316793fe64ae, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Exactly! So you have to connect your sand before the mud connects
      itself.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB9DE\uC544\uC694! \uADF8\uB7EC\uB2C8 \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC5EC\uC11C
      \uC11C\uB85C\uB97C \uC787\uAE30 \uC804\uC5D0, \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB85C
      \uC11C\uB85C\uB97C \uC774\uC5B4\uC57C \uD574\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce46d5e3f69096f4a84f9897353ff324, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Line up five or more squares in a row, across, down, or diagonally,
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uAC00\uB85C, \uC138\uB85C, \uB300\uAC01\uC120 \uBC29\uD5A5\uC73C\uB85C
      5\uCE78 \uC774\uC0C1\uC744 \uC5F0\uC18D\uC73C\uB85C \uC774\uC73C\uBA74"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b01f092eb0545574db7d43f93e64aba7, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: and you'll shock the ground hard enough before the mud can pile
      up.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC774\uAE30 \uC804\uC5D0 \uB545\uC5D0
      \uCDA9\uBD84\uD55C \uC790\uADF9\uC744 \uC904 \uC218 \uC788\uC744 \uAC70\uC608\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 312af029b1b084a41ade9a6fdf1a6418, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: But once you've shocked the ground, the oasis sand gets absorbed
      right into it,
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uD558\uC9C0\uB9CC \uC790\uADF9\uC744 \uC8FC\uACE0 \uB09C \uD6C4
      \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB294 \uB545\uC73C\uB85C \uD761\uC218\uB418\uC5B4\uBC84\uB9AC\uACE0,"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a27f087f63d32394aa6a316793fe64ae, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: and mud can settle on top and plug the well. So be careful.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uADF8 \uC704\uB85C \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uB0B4\uB824\uC549\uC544
      \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC774 \uB9C9\uD600\uBC84\uB9B4 \uC218\uB3C4 \uC788\uC73C\uB2C8
      \uC870\uC2EC\uD574."
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 804f4937427d73c438fd059b9f112a8f, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Here's a tip. As long as a square is more than half oasis sand,
      a little mud mixed in doesn't matter!
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC774\uAC74 \uD301\uC778\uB370, \uD55C \uCE78\uC758 \uBC18
      \uC774\uC0C1\uB9CC \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB85C \uCC44\uC6B0\uBA74
      \uADF8 \uCE78\uC740 \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC870\uAE08 \uC11E\uC5EC\uB3C4 \uC0C1\uAD00\uC5C6\uB300\uC694!"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce46d5e3f69096f4a84f9897353ff324, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Four or fewer and the line's worthless, sadly,
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC544\uC27D\uAC8C\uB3C4 4\uCE78 \uC774\uD558\uB85C\uB9CC \uC787\uACE0
      \uB04A\uAE30\uBA74 \uBB34\uC6A9\uC9C0\uBB3C\uC774\uC9C0\uB9CC,"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b01f092eb0545574db7d43f93e64aba7, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: but past five, the longer you run it, the faster the well wakes
      up!
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "5\uCE78 \uC774\uC0C1\uC774\uBA74 \uC5F0\uC18D\uC73C\uB85C \uB354
      \uAE38\uAC8C \uC774\uC744\uC218\uB85D \uBE68\uB9AC \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC744 \uB6AB\uC744
      \uC218 \uC788\uC744 \uAC70\uC608\uC694!"
    portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 312af029b1b084a41ade9a6fdf1a6418, type: 3}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
